IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cat-domain`
IMPORT `cat-time`
IMPORT `cat-part1-preliminary`
IMPORT `tests-fixtures`

-- TESTS — time (Interpretation Act ss 61, 62) and Part 1 of the Cat Act.
-- Every expected value is worked from the source text, and the working is
-- in the comment beside it. A failing assertion is a finding: do not edit
-- an expected value to make it pass.

§ `Tests — time and Part 1`

§§ `The period the encoding answers for`

#ASSERT `the law is encoded for` (YMD 2025 9 25)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the law is encoded for` (YMD 2025 9 24)
        BECAUSE "no source is encoded for a date before 25 September 2025: this encoding states the Cat Act 2011 as consolidated from 25 September 2025 and the Cat Regulations 2012 as consolidated from 24 July 2025"

§§ `Interpretation Act s 62 — reaching an age`

-- s 62(3)'s own example: "a period of 6 months beginning on 30 or 31 August
-- ends on 28 February". So a cat born 31 Aug 2025 has NOT reached 6 months
-- on 28 Feb 2026 and HAS on 1 Mar 2026.
#ASSERT NOT `reached` 6 `months of age, if born on` (YMD 2025 8 31) `, on` (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT     `reached` 6 `months of age, if born on` (YMD 2025 8 31) `, on` (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- s 62(2)'s example: a month beginning on 15 January ends on 14 February.
-- Six months beginning 15 Jan 2026 end 14 Jul 2026; reached on 15 Jul.
#ASSERT NOT `reached` 6 `months of age, if born on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, on` (YMD 2026 7 14)
#ASSERT     `reached` 6 `months of age, if born on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, on` (YMD 2026 7 15)
-- Bea, born 1 June 2012, is under 18 until the end of 31 May 2030.
#ASSERT     `under` 18 `years of age, if born on` (YMD 2012 6 1) `, on` (YMD 2030 5 31)
#ASSERT NOT `under` 18 `years of age, if born on` (YMD 2012 6 1) `, on` (YMD 2030 6 1)
-- Born 29 Feb 2008: 216 months beginning that day have no corresponding
-- date in Feb 2026, so they run to 28 Feb 2026; 18 is reached on 1 Mar 2026.
#ASSERT     `under` 18 `years of age, if born on` (YMD 2008 2 29) `, on` (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT NOT `under` 18 `years of age, if born on` (YMD 2008 2 29) `, on` (YMD 2026 3 1)

§§ `Interpretation Act s 61 — within n days after`

-- 7 days after Mon 1 Dec 2025, excluding 1 Dec: ends Mon 8 Dec, a working day.
#ASSERT `the last day to act within` 7 `days after` (YMD 2025 12 1) `given` `WA holidays 2025-26` EQUALS YMD 2025 12 8
-- 7 days after Thu 18 Dec 2025 ends Thu 25 Dec (Christmas Day, excluded);
-- 26 Dec Boxing Day, 27 Sat, 28 Sun are excluded too: s 61(1)(e) moves it to Mon 29 Dec.
#ASSERT `the last day to act within` 7 `days after` (YMD 2025 12 18) `given` `WA holidays 2025-26` EQUALS YMD 2025 12 29
-- With no holidays supplied, 25 Dec is a Thursday and stands.
#ASSERT `the last day to act within` 7 `days after` (YMD 2025 12 18) `given` `no holidays` EQUALS YMD 2025 12 25

§§ `Working days (fork F-01)`

-- 3 working days after Fri 5 Dec 2025: Mon 8, Tue 9, Wed 10.
#ASSERT `the date` 3 `working days after` (YMD 2025 12 5) `given` `WA holidays 2025-26` EQUALS YMD 2025 12 10
-- 3 working days after Wed 24 Dec 2025: 25, 26 holidays; 27, 28 weekend;
-- Mon 29 (1), Tue 30 (2), Wed 31 (3).
#ASSERT `the date` 3 `working days after` (YMD 2025 12 24) `given` `WA holidays 2025-26` EQUALS YMD 2025 12 31
#ASSERT NOT `a working day` (YMD 2026 3 2) `given` `WA holidays 2025-26`      -- Labour Day
#ASSERT     `a working day` (YMD 2026 3 3) `given` `WA holidays 2025-26`

§§ `Within the n months before (fork F-02)`

-- A conviction on 10 Jan 2023 is within the 36 months before 9 Jan 2026,
-- and outside them on 10 Jan 2026 (the anniversary itself — fork F-02).
#ASSERT     `within the` 36 `months before` (YMD 2026 1 9)  `, an event on` (YMD 2023 1 10)
#ASSERT NOT `within the` 36 `months before` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, an event on` (YMD 2023 1 10)
#ASSERT NOT `within the` 36 `months before` (YMD 2026 1 9)  `, an event on` (YMD 2026 1 10)   -- after the day

§§ `s 3(1) — cat management facility, reg 4`

#ASSERT     `prescribed as an operator of a facility for keeping cats` `Cat Welfare Society Inc., trading as Cat Haven`
#ASSERT     `prescribed as an operator of a facility for keeping cats` `The Royal Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals, Western Australia`
#ASSERT NOT `prescribed as an operator of a facility for keeping cats` `Saving Animals from Euthanasia Incorporated`
#ASSERT     `a cat management facility` (Facility WITH `used, or may be used, for keeping cats` IS TRUE,  `operator` IS `operated by a local government`)
#ASSERT NOT `a cat management facility` (Facility WITH `used, or may be used, for keeping cats` IS FALSE, `operator` IS `operated by a local government`)
#ASSERT     `a cat management facility` (Facility WITH `used, or may be used, for keeping cats` IS TRUE,  `operator` IS `operated by an organisation` `Cat Welfare Society Inc., trading as Cat Haven`)
#ASSERT NOT `a cat management facility` (Facility WITH `used, or may be used, for keeping cats` IS TRUE,  `operator` IS `operated by an organisation` `another organisation`)
#ASSERT     `a cat management facility` (Facility WITH `used, or may be used, for keeping cats` IS TRUE,  `operator` IS `operated by a person or body approved in writing by a local government`)
#ASSERT NOT `a cat management facility` (Facility WITH `used, or may be used, for keeping cats` IS TRUE,  `operator` IS `operated by another person or body`)

§§ `s 3(1) — microchip database company, reg 6`

#ASSERT     `prescribed as a microchip database company` `Central Animal Records (Aust) Pty Ltd`
#ASSERT     `prescribed as a microchip database company` `Global Microchip Registry Pty Ltd, trading as Global Micro Animal Registry`
#ASSERT     `prescribed as a microchip database company` `PetBase Pty Ltd, trading as Petsafe`
#ASSERT     `prescribed as a microchip database company` `Royal Agricultural Society of NSW, trading as Australasian Animal Registry`
#ASSERT NOT `prescribed as a microchip database company` `another organisation`
#ASSERT     `a microchip database company` `PetBase Pty Ltd, trading as Petsafe` `keeping a database:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a microchip database company` `PetBase Pty Ltd, trading as Petsafe` `keeping a database:` FALSE

§§ `s 3(1) — microchip implanter, reg 7`

#ASSERT     `a microchip implanter` `the vet`                                                                                                -- reg 7(1)(a)
#ASSERT     `a microchip implanter` (`an implanter: vet` FALSE `, nurse` TRUE  `, units` EMPTY `, courses` EMPTY)                               -- reg 7(1)(b)
#ASSERT     `a microchip implanter` (`an implanter: vet` FALSE `, nurse` FALSE `, units` (LIST "ACMMIC401")  `, courses` (LIST "ACM40412"))       -- 7(2)(a)(ii) + (b)(i)
#ASSERT     `a microchip implanter` (`an implanter: vet` FALSE `, nurse` FALSE `, units` (LIST "ACMMIC401A") `, courses` (LIST "ACMSS00001"))     -- 7(2)(a)(i) + (b)(iva)
#ASSERT NOT `a microchip implanter` (`an implanter: vet` FALSE `, nurse` FALSE `, units` (LIST "ACMMIC401")  `, courses` EMPTY)                -- (b) missing: "and"
#ASSERT NOT `a microchip implanter` (`an implanter: vet` FALSE `, nurse` FALSE `, units` EMPTY               `, courses` (LIST "ACM40310"))     -- (a) missing
#ASSERT NOT `a microchip implanter` (`an implanter: vet` FALSE `, nurse` FALSE `, units` (LIST "XYZ001")     `, courses` (LIST "ACM40310"))     -- not a listed unit
#ASSERT NOT `a microchip implanter` `Alex`

§§ `s 3(1) — microchip, microchipped, sterilised; regs 5, 8`

#ASSERT     `microchipped` `Alex's unregistered cat`
-- A device complying with AS 5018 but not AS 5019 is not of the prescribed
-- type: reg 5(1) requires "both".
#ASSERT NOT `of a prescribed type` (`Implanted device` WITH
                                       `capable of being implanted in a cat` IS TRUE
                                       `designed to record information that can be electronically retrieved` IS TRUE
                                       `complies with AS 5018-2001` IS TRUE
                                       `complies with AS 5019-2001` IS FALSE
                                       `implanted by` IS `the vet`
                                       `date implanted` IS YMD 2024 3 1)
-- reg 8: implanted by someone who is not a microchip implanter — not "microchipped".
#ASSERT NOT `microchipped` (`a Perth cat born` (YMD 2024 1 1) `kept by` EMPTY `registered` NOTHING
                              `chipped` (JUST (`a compliant microchip implanted by` `Alex` `on` (YMD 2024 3 1)))
                              `desexed` NOTHING)
#ASSERT     `sterilised` `Alex's unregistered cat`
#ASSERT NOT `sterilised` `the August kitten`

§§ `s 3(1) registered — reg 12(2)(a)`

-- (i) one year: "until ... the next 31 October".
#ASSERT `the last day of the registration period` (`registered with` "City of Perth" `to` "Alex" `for` `one year` `from` (YMD 2025 11 1))  EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 31)
#ASSERT `the last day of the registration period` (`registered with` "City of Perth" `to` "Alex" `for` `one year` `from` (YMD 2026 3 15))  EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 31)
-- fork F-03: from 31 October itself, the next 31 October is a year on.
#ASSERT `the last day of the registration period` (`registered with` "City of Perth" `to` "Alex" `for` `one year` `from` (YMD 2025 10 31)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 31)
-- (ii) 3 years, fork F-04: the third 31 October.
#ASSERT `the last day of the registration period` (`registered with` "City of Perth" `to` "Alex" `for` `3 years` `from` (YMD 2025 11 1))   EQUALS JUST (YMD 2028 10 31)
-- (iii) life: until the death of the cat — no fixed last day.
#ASSERT `the last day of the registration period` (`registered with` "City of Perth" `to` "Alex" `for` `the life of the cat` `from` (YMD 2025 11 1)) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT     `registered` `Alex's registered cat` `on` (YMD 2025 12 1)
#ASSERT     `registered` `Alex's registered cat` `on` (YMD 2026 10 31)
#ASSERT NOT `registered` `Alex's registered cat` `on` (YMD 2026 11 1)
#ASSERT NOT `registered` `Alex's registered cat` `on` (YMD 2025 10 31)    -- before it took effect
#ASSERT NOT `registered` `Alex's unregistered cat` `on` (YMD 2025 12 1)

§§ `s 4 — owner`

-- (a) a registered cat: the registered owner.
#ASSERT `the owners of` `Alex's registered cat` `on` (YMD 2025 12 1) `, evidence to the contrary of the database record being` FALSE EQUALS LIST "Alex"
-- (b) unregistered: whoever ordinarily keeps and cares for it.
#ASSERT `the owners of` `Alex's unregistered cat` `on` (YMD 2025 12 1) `, evidence to the contrary of the database record being` FALSE EQUALS LIST "Alex"
-- (b) and (c): kept by a child, Bea (13); her guardian Carl is an owner too (fork F-05).
`Bea's cat` MEANS
    `a Perth cat born` (YMD 2024 1 1) `kept by` (LIST `kept by` `Bea` `since` (YMD 2025 1 1))
        `registered` NOTHING `chipped` NOTHING `desexed` NOTHING
#ASSERT `the owners of` `Bea's cat` `on` (YMD 2025 12 1) `, evidence to the contrary of the database record being` FALSE EQUALS LIST "Bea", "Carl"
#ASSERT `an owner of` `Bea's cat` `on` (YMD 2025 12 1) `:` `Carl`
#ASSERT NOT `an owner of` `Bea's cat` `on` (YMD 2025 12 1) `:` `Alex`
-- (2) unregistered but microchipped: the database's recorded owner is taken
-- to keep the cat "in the absence of evidence to the contrary".
`Dana's database cat` MEANS
    Cat WITH
        `name`                                     IS "Ginger"
        `date of birth`                            IS YMD 2024 1 1
        `district where ordinarily kept`           IS "City of Perth"
        `kept in the State`                        IS TRUE
        `date of death`                            IS NOTHING
        `registration`                             IS NOTHING
        `registered with another local government since` IS FALSE
        `implanted device`                         IS JUST (`a compliant microchip implanted by` `the vet` `on` (YMD 2024 3 1))
        `sterilising procedure`                    IS NOTHING
        `certificate against microchipping`        IS NOTHING
        `certificate against sterilisation`        IS NOTHING
        `keepings`                                 IS LIST `kept by` `Alex` `since` (YMD 2025 10 15)
        `name recorded as owner in a microchip database` IS JUST "Dana"
        `custodian`                                IS NOTHING
        `foster placement`                         IS NOTHING
        `owned for the purpose of breeding`        IS FALSE
        `sterilisation tattoo on the ear`          IS FALSE
#ASSERT `the owners of` `Dana's database cat` `on` (YMD 2025 12 1) `, evidence to the contrary of the database record being` FALSE EQUALS LIST "Alex", "Dana"
#ASSERT `the owners of` `Dana's database cat` `on` (YMD 2025 12 1) `, evidence to the contrary of the database record being` TRUE  EQUALS LIST "Alex"
-- Before the keeping began (15 Oct 2025), Alex did not keep the cat.
#ASSERT `the owners of` `Dana's database cat` `on` (YMD 2025 10 14) `, evidence to the contrary of the database record being` FALSE EQUALS LIST "Dana"

§§ `s 3(1) authorised person`

#ASSERT     `an authorised person` (Officer WITH `authorisation` IS `a police officer`, `an employee of the local government` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT     `an authorised person` (Officer WITH `authorisation` IS `designated under the Public Health Act 2016 s 24(1) for the purposes of the Cat Act`, `an employee of the local government` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT     `an authorised person` (Officer WITH `authorisation` IS `appointed under the Local Government Act 1995 s 9.10(2) for the purposes of the Cat Act`, `an employee of the local government` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `an authorised person` (Officer WITH `authorisation` IS `no authorisation under the Cat Act`, `an employee of the local government` IS TRUE)
